¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙa people great, and many, and tall, as the Anakims; but the LORD destroyed them before them; and they succeeded them, and dwelt in their stead:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¬as he did to the children of Esau, which dwelt in Seir, when he destroyed the Horims from before them; and they succeeded them, and dwelt in their stead even unto this day:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’and the Avims which dwelt in Hazerim, even unto Azzah, the Caphtorims, which came forth out of Caphtor, destroyed them, and dwelt in their stead.)¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÉRise ye up, take your journey, and pass over the river Arnon: behold, I have given into thine hand Sihon the Amorite, king of Heshbon, and his land: begin to possess it, and contend with him in battle.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÊThis day will I begin to put the dread of thee and the fear of thee upon the nations that are under the whole heaven, who shall hear report of thee, and shall tremble, and be in anguish because of thee.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoAnd I sent messengers out of the wilderness of Kedemoth unto Sihon king of Heshbon with words of peace, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwLet me pass through thy land: I will go along by the high way, I will neither turn unto the right hand nor to the left.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†Thou shalt sell me meat for money, that I may eat; and give me water for money, that I may drink: only I will pass through on my feet;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ®(as the children of Esau which dwell in Seir, and the Moabites which dwell in Ar, did unto me;) until I shall pass over Jordan into the land which the LORD our God giveth us.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¿But Sihon king of Heshbon would not let us pass by him: for the LORD thy God hardened his spirit, and made his heart obstinate, that he might deliver him into thy hand, as appeareth this day.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse%¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒAnd the LORD said unto me, Behold, I have begun to give Sihon and his land before thee: begin to possess, that thou mayest inherit his land.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙIThen Sihon came out against us, he and all his people, to fight at Jahaz.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaAnd the LORD our God delivered him before us; and we smote him, and his sons, and all his people.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’And we took all his cities at that time, and utterly destroyed the men, and the women, and the little ones, of every city, we left none to remain:¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]only the cattle we took for a prey unto ourselves, and the spoil of the cities which we took.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÄFrom Aroer, which is by the brink of the river of Arnon, and from the city that is by the river, even unto Gilead, there was not one city too strong for us: the LORD our God delivered all unto us:¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙºonly unto the land of the children of Ammon thou camest not, nor unto any place of the river Jabbok, nor unto the cities in the mountains, nor unto whatsoever the LORD our God forbad us.¦layout ªlast_verse%